                        "entry_id": "4f76bfce-cb57-32c2-91b5-f017a7a3d087",
                        "glosses": [
                            "книжн. связанный, соотносящийся по значению с существительным элегия"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "07e14a8b-faeb-3e7b-b537-e646513b78a9",
                        "entry_id": "4f76bfce-cb57-32c2-91b5-f017a7a3d087",
                        "glosses": [
                            "свойственный произведениям жанра элегии, характерный для них"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "14dd96c1-4670-37a8-a1ab-22a69a8a619f",
                        "entry_id": "4f76bfce-cb57-32c2-91b5-f017a7a3d087",
                        "glosses": [
                            "перен. грустно-мечтательный, меланхолический"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "53273a78-3783-4a46-a68a-310db82df6ed",
                                "sense_id": "14dd96c1-4670-37a8-a1ab-22a69a8a619f",
                                "text": "Парикмахер был немолодой человек с добрыми воспалёнными глазами и элегической улыбкой на рыжем лице."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6354036f-520e-45b8-be09-fe1ee1bc1c0e",
                        "source_entry_id": "4f76bfce-cb57-32c2-91b5-f017a7a3d087",
                        "target_lang_word": "elegiac",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "elegiac",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a1c91d0d-b466-3cc0-8789-eabbde371ffd",
                                        "entry_id": "f2b05917-7533-3dd5-8981-0a56f300b91f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of or relating to an elegy."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "21c30392-f56b-468b-bd42-87230ac9b2cb",
                                                "sense_id": "a1c91d0d-b466-3cc0-8789-eabbde371ffd",
                                                "text": "the elegiac distich or couplet, consisting of a dactylic hexameter and pentameter"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2ea37d88-d093-3fbd-9044-f27ed53d128e",
                                        "entry_id": "f2b05917-7533-3dd5-8981-0a56f300b91f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Expressing sorrow or mourning."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c4386409-9861-4cad-817c-a6cb07c4ab26",
                                                "sense_id": "2ea37d88-d093-3fbd-9044-f27ed53d128e",
                                                "text": "Hast thou no elegiac verse / For Brunswick's venerable hearse, / What! not a line, a tear, a sigh, / When valour bleeds for liberty?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "625f2755-8fda-424a-bbc3-df0bc24fec0b",
                                                "sense_id": "2ea37d88-d093-3fbd-9044-f27ed53d128e",
                                                "text": "And elegiac griefs, and songs of love,"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "elegiac",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "86fa0324-c064-3341-b5cc-fa2659d8565e",
                                        "entry_id": "2719a676-a264-3742-87f8-a6b554b7d5b1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A poem composed in the couplet style of classical elegies: a line of dactylic hexameter followed by a line of dactylic pentameter."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7c98104c-d443-431f-9160-32daef36d640",
                                                "sense_id": "86fa0324-c064-3341-b5cc-fa2659d8565e",
                                                "text": "His saphics are worse, if possible, than his elegiacs"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
